media: h713-hdmirx: no LINK read after the standby parked the MIPS

The audio poll reads the receiver's LINK window every 100 ms on
system_wq, and nothing stopped it for a standby to RAM. cpu_comm parks
the MIPS in its suspend_late and genpd powers TVFE and TVCAP off in the
noirq phase; what the firmware had set up in the receiver does not come
back with the power, and the parked MIPS sets nothing up again. A LINK
read in that state does not answer zero, it stops the bus. On the HY310
(08.10.2026, breadcrumbs in the RTC general purpose words, kept over the
watchdog reset):

  L-B   poll running:  read 4 begun after resume_noirq, never finished
  L-A 2 poll paused, back 3 s after the wake: the resume completed
        (rc=0, 0.56 s), read 1 of the poll begun, never finished,
        SoC watchdog reset 16 s later

The poll now stops in the suspend callback. The resume asks cpu_comm
whether the firmware still runs: after a sleep aborted before the park
the poll comes back; after the park this instance never reads LINK
again, empties the three audio controls and says so once. The status
and hdcp files report "not read" instead of reading. h713-mips-restart
unbinds the receiver around the restart, and the new instance's probe
starts the poll. A probe while the MIPS is parked or stopped does not
start it either. The comment that called the reads safe while the block
sleeps is marked as overtaken.

Compiled out of tree against the R1 kernel with W=1, no warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
